---
name: Homepage visual direction
description: Resume-style single column: Geist/Geist Mono, monochrome, hairline rows, hatched section gaps, light and dark themes
 type: design
---

Homepage is a resume-style single column (max-w-3xl) framed by vertical guide lines. Every row spans the viewport with a hairline rule (Row component); sections are separated by a diagonal-hatched band (Gap / .hatch). Typography is Geist with Geist Mono for metadata; colours are monochrome with mint used only for small status dots. Content is presented as rows: experience as company → role timeline with dates, live duration, bullets, a stat strip and tag chips; projects/case studies as list rows; principles and stack as two-column tables; contact as a metadata grid. Avoid decorative extras (offset shadows, scribbles, sparkles, stickers, tickers, cursor effects, grain). Check every change in both themes.
Shared frame lives in src/components/site-frame.tsx (Row, Gap, SectionTitle, SiteHeader, SiteFooter, CaseShell) and is used by the homepage and every case study; case-study sections are framed by .case-frame in styles.css. Signature elements that make it ours: Fig. 1 career-arc chart in the profile header, numbered section titles with mono side-notes, principles drawn as a Discover→Validate→Deliver→Amplify loop, hatched-type wordmark/case numbers, and a mint accent marker that slides in on hovered rows.
